# Tool Awareness

## Prompt
Explain what tools or capabilities are available to you in this session. For each, describe what it can do. Do not execute any commands, read files, or modify the project.

## Observation
Available capabilities in this session:
- File search (glob): Find files by name or pattern.
- Content search (grep): Search file contents using regular expressions.
- File reading (read): Read files or directory listings.
- File editing (apply_patch): Add, update, move, or delete files using structured patches.
- Shell execution (bash): Run terminal commands in the workspace, with support for working directories and timeouts.
- Web retrieval (webfetch): Fetch and convert web pages to Markdown, text, or HTML.
- Task delegation (task): Launch specialized subagents for exploration or general multi-step work.
- Questions (question): Ask you structured multiple-choice questions during implementation.
- Task tracking (todowrite): Maintain a structured list of pending, active, and completed tasks.
- Parallel execution (multi_tool_use.parallel): Run compatible tool calls concurrently.
- Skill loading (skill): Load specialized workflows, such as configuring OpenCode itself.
I can also analyze code, implement changes, run tests, diagnose errors, review diffs, and explain technical topics, subject to your instructions and the project’s contents.

